### Component 2: Backend Validation & Error Handling

To make the Express server robust against malicious or invalid inputs, we will integrate Zod schemas and global Express middleware:

#### [NEW] validation middleware: [validate.js](file:///c:/CODING/Wed%20development/SplitWise/backend/middleware/validate.js)
Define an Express middleware function `validateBody(schema)`, `validateQuery(schema)`, `validateParams(schema)` that validates input using Zod and returns standardized `400 Bad Request` validation error responses when validation fails.

#### [NEW] input schemas: `backend/validation/*.js`
Define Zod validation schemas for all key endpoints:
- **Auth schemas:** `loginSchema`, `registerSchema`, `forgotPasswordSchema`, `resetPasswordSchema`
- **Expense schemas:** `createExpenseSchema` (checking description, amount > 0, valid groupId, paidBy, splitType, and splits matching members list)
- **Group schemas:** `createGroupSchema` (checking name is non-empty, and members list has at least one member)

#### [NEW] centralized error handler: [errorHandler.js](file:///c:/CODING/Wed%20development/SplitWise/backend/middleware/errorHandler.js)
Catch all uncaught exceptions (`500 Internal Server Error`), database connectivity failures, or operational errors in one place. It will log the stack trace to console or file, and return clean JSON response payloads:
`{ "error": "Internal Server Error", "message": "..." }`

#### [MODIFY] [server.js](file:///c:/CODING/Wed%20development/SplitWise/backend/server.js)
Register the `errorHandler` middleware at the very end of the routing chain.

#### [MODIFY] Integrate middleware in routes: `backend/routes/*.js`
Modify route handlers to import schemas and register the validation middleware before handler execution (e.g., `router.post('/register', validateBody(registerSchema), registerHandler)`).

